"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[42526],{42526:function(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"content":"\\n<center>\\n<BookCard \\n          cover=\\"/assets/snippets/books/PleaseFindMyBody.png\\"\\n          title=\\"Please Find My Body\\"\\n          author=\\"Hoshizuki Wataru\\"\\n          publisher=\\"Banta\\"\\n          publishedDate=\\"2025-07-28\\"\\n          isbn=\\"9791194930372\\"\\n          rating=3.5\\n          tags=\\"mystery\\"\\n        />\\n</center>\\n\\n## Review\\nIt is often said that the first sentence or first chapter is everything in a novel.  \\nIn that sense, I think this novel is successful at least in its opening part.  \\n\\nJust before disappearing, a bestselling mystery writer leaves a single sentence on his `blog`: <mark>Please find my body</mark>.  \\nThis single sentence, which is no different from a suicide note, becomes the bait that runs through the entire novel.  \\n\\nHowever, even after the writer disappears, posts keep appearing on the blog.  \\nAnd they are posts that <mark>expose the secrets of surrounding people one by one</mark>.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nIs this person alive or dead? Who on earth is writing these posts?  \\nAnd what does that person\'s secret have to do with the disappearance?  \\n\\nWhile reading, these question marks kept piling up in my head, naturally leading me to flip to the next page.  \\nFor this introduction alone, I want to give this novel a <mark>high score</mark>.  \\n\\nHowever, the disappointments were also clear.  \\nAs it progressed to the second half, there were constant moments where I thought, ```Did the stage really need to be set to this extent?```  \\nEvery event and character behavior fit perfectly within the writer\'s big picture without a single error, but that actually felt like a <mark>leap of logic</mark>.  \\nThere were too many coincidences that felt absolutely impossible to align so perfectly in reality.  \\n```adcard\\n```\\nThe way the protagonist\'s emotions were narrated was also disappointing.  \\n\\nThere were many sentences that simply <mark>explained</mark> rather than showed the character\'s psychology.  \\nNarrations like ```I felt this way at this time``` were repeated, which broke the immersion bit by bit.  \\n\\nI suppose it was inevitable in trying to explain the complex plot typical of a mystery.  \\nStill, I was left wishing that emotions could have been shown in a more sophisticated way.  \\n\\nOverall, it gave the impression of a typical mystery novel where <mark>characters move exactly as planned on a well-constructed stage</mark>, which is a characteristic of conventional mystery novels.  \\nWhile it is certainly fun to read, it is a novel where the plot takes precedence over the characters.  \\n\\nI thought that this style might actually mask these shortcomings better if it were adapted into a screen version, and indeed, it is said to have been produced as a drama of the same name.  \\nSince explanatory psychological depictions would be reduced and the tension could be filled with visuals and editing, it might be a story better suited for the screen."}')}}]);